{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BalancedGenerators","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BalancedGenerators","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SkeinFromHecke"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.negCrossing_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.negCrossing_one","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L271-L276","doc":"At `q = qi = 1` each generator is its own inverse: the negative crossing is the\npositive one, which is exactly the statement that the braiding has degenerated to a\nsymmetry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.sigma_sq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.sigma_sq_one","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L265-L269","doc":"At `q = qi = 1`, `σ_i² = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.liftBalanced_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.liftBalanced_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L241-L254","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.liftBalanced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.liftBalanced","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L225-L239","doc":"**The balanced universal property.** A family satisfying the §7a relations — the\nsymmetric quadratic and the braid relation — extends to an algebra map out of `H(M, q²)`\nsending `σ_i` to it.\n\nThe hypothesis is stated in the normalisation a representation of this framework is\nactually written in, so a consumer never has to perform the rescaling by hand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.hom_ext_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.hom_ext_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L217-L223","doc":"**Maps out of the algebra are determined by the balanced generators.** Since\n`T_i = q σ_i`, agreeing on the `σ_i` is the same as agreeing on the `T_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.sigma_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.sigma_braid","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L208-L215","doc":"**The braid relation transfers.** Rescaling every generator by the same central scalar\nleaves the braid relation intact: both sides pick up the same power of `qi`, because\n`altProd` on the two sides has the same number of factors exactly when `M` is symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.sigma_eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.sigma_eigen","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L199-L204","doc":"**The eigenvalue factorisation** `(σ_i − q)(σ_i + qi) = 0`: the symmetric channel has\neigenvalue `q` and the antisymmetric channel `−qi`, as AGENTS.md §7a states. This is the\nstatement that fails in the Iwahori normalisation, where the eigenvalues are `q²` and `−1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.sigma_sub_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.sigma_sub_inv","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L191-L197","doc":"**The skein relation** `σ_i − σ_i⁻¹ = q − qi`, i.e. `L₊ − L₋ = (q − qi) L₀` with the\nsmoothing `L₀ = 1`. Stated against an *arbitrary* right inverse: a right inverse of `σ_i`\nhas no choice but to be the negative crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.sigmaUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.sigmaUnit","kind":"def","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L187-L189","doc":"`σ_i` as a unit, with its inverse given explicitly rather than existentially. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.isUnit_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.isUnit_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L182-L185","doc":"**`σ_i` is a unit** — which is what makes `H(M, q²)` a quotient of the *braid group*\nalgebra rather than merely of the free algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.negCrossing_mul_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.negCrossing_mul_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L178-L180","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.sigma_mul_negCrossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.sigma_mul_negCrossing","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L173-L176","doc":"**The negative crossing** `σ_i⁻¹ = σ_i − (q − qi)` is a two-sided inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.T_eq_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.T_eq_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L159-L164","doc":"The Iwahori generator recovered from the balanced one: `T_i = q σ_i`. This is what\nmakes the rescaling a change of *generators* rather than a passage to a subalgebra — the\n`σ_i` generate everything the `T_i` do. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.isHeckeGenerator_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.isHeckeGenerator_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L148-L157","doc":"**The bridge.** The rescaled generator satisfies the *symmetric* Hecke quadratic\nrelation of AGENTS.md §7a:\n\n    σ_i² = (q − qi) σ_i + 1.\n\nEverything in `QOU.MathlibExt.SkeinRelation` applies to `σ_i` from here on: the explicit\nnegative crossing, invertibility, the skein relation, and the eigenvalue factorisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.sigma","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L142-L144","doc":"**The §7a generator** `σ_i = qi·T_i`, in the symmetric (skein) normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.BalancedHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.BalancedHecke","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L138-L140","doc":"The Iwahori–Hecke algebra at the **squared** parameter `Q = q²`. Squaring is what makes\nthe balanced rescaling `σ = qi·T` land on the §7a eigenvalues `q`, `−qi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.altProd_algebraMap_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.altProd_algebraMap_mul","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L112-L130","doc":"**Rescaling by a central scalar multiplies `altProd` by its power.**\n`altProd (r·a) (r·b) n = rⁿ · altProd a b n`. The alternation is invisible to a central\nscalar: each of the `n` factors contributes exactly one `r`, whichever of `a`, `b` it is.\n\nThis is what carries the braid relation across the rescaling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.iwahori_of_isHeckeGenerator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.iwahori_of_isHeckeGenerator","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L102-L110","doc":"**Balanced ⟹ Iwahori.** If `x` satisfies `x² = (q − qi)x + 1` then `q·x` satisfies the\nIwahori relation at the squared parameter, `(qx − q²)(qx + 1) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.isHeckeGenerator_of_iwahori","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.isHeckeGenerator_of_iwahori","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean#L83-L100","doc":"**Iwahori ⟹ balanced.** If `y` satisfies `(y − q²)(y + 1) = 0` then `qi·y` satisfies\nthe symmetric relation `x² = (q − qi)x + 1`.\n\nStated for an arbitrary element of an arbitrary `R`-algebra: the rescaling is a fact about\nthe two quadratics, not about the Hecke algebra. ","signatureChunk":0}]}